⚡ European Intraday Electricity Market Forecasting Engine
AI-Based 15-Minute Electricity Price Forecasting

An end-to-end machine learning project for forecasting European intraday electricity prices using historical market data, feature engineering and gradient boosting models.

The project demonstrates the complete workflow of an intraday forecasting engine, from raw market data processing to model training, recursive forecasting, backtesting and interactive visualization.

📌 Project Objective

Intraday electricity markets are highly dynamic, with prices changing every 15 minutes due to:

Renewable generation variability
Electricity demand fluctuations
Weather conditions
Grid congestion
Cross-border market coupling

The objective of this project is to build a machine learning pipeline capable of forecasting the next 24 hours of intraday electricity prices (96 × 15-minute intervals) across multiple European markets.

🌍 Markets Covered

The forecasting engine supports:

🇩🇪 Germany
🇫🇷 France
🇮🇹 Italy
🇳🇱 Netherlands
🇪🇸 Spain

Historical data covers approximately 2020–2026.

⚠️ Repository Notice

To keep the repository lightweight, the following folders are not included:

data/
models/

These folders contain large datasets, trained machine learning models and generated forecasts whose combined size exceeds GitHub's recommended repository limits.

All source code required to recreate these folders is included in the src/ directory.

